From 41d8e720d17e853556de06c3827f017acfb7ff12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:35:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/21] compiler: z/OS support needed by the run time library

- main is a stub with argc/argv/envp that calls FPC_SYSTEMMAIN (as on AIX)
- C library functions are called by their external names in ASCII mode:
  the z/OS headers map many functions with #pragma map (fopen is @@A00246).
  The table is read from zosmap.txt in the unit search path (generated
  from the z/OS headers, see zos-pascal-llvm: scripts/gen-zosmap.py)
- functions referenced only through a code pointer (e.g. the unit
  initialisation routines in the INITFINAL table) are declared as
  functions: GOFF distinguishes code and data symbols, and the address of
  a function stored in data must be a function descriptor
- LLVM metadata parameters of intrinsics do not occupy an argument slot
- weak external symbols are supported
- get_frame is supported (LLVM frameaddress)

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
